    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The other summand in these costs, E[ 0 T(X(s) − ζ(s))⊤Ξ(s)(X(s) − ζ(s))ds], can be used to incorporate some kind of risk preference into the model via the choice of the matrix-valued process Ξ, which acts as a penalization, and the Rn-valued process ζ, which acts as a running target. We refer to Horst & Xia [36, Section 1.1] for an illustrative example of a possible choice for Ξ. The risk term is a further possible source of crosseffects in our model, since Ξ does not need to be diagonal."
